            <person xml:id="HAL04" sex="1">
               <persName>
                  <forename>Robert</forename>
                  <surname>Hall</surname>
               </persName>
               <birth when="1764-05-02"/>
               <death when="1831-02-21"/>
               <occupation>Baptist Minister</occupation>
               <note type="editorial">
                  <p>Robert Hall was a Baptist Minister who spent time at Cambridge, Leicester and
                     Bristol preaching. In 1800 Godwin read a number of sermons delivered by Robert
                     Hall. Hall was also a lifelong friend of <persName key="MAC01">James
                        Mackintosh</persName>, explaining his presence at dinner at Mackintosh’s.
                  </p>
               </note>
